_REGISTRY: dict[str, list[Callable]] = {}

def register_rule_check(rule_id):
    def decorator(fn):
        _REGISTRY.setdefault(rule_id, []).append(fn)
        return fn
    return decorator

def get_checks_for_rule(rule_id):
    return _REGISTRY.get(rule_id, [])
Used only by rule-specific checks (rule1_checks.py, rule2_checks.py, rule3_checks.py) — the 13 generic checks bypass the registry entirely, living as plain functions in their category files and called unconditionally via a GENERIC_CHECKS list. Category stays a file-location/documentation concept, not something the registry itself tracks.